From 48e7295f4522ea9f9edf52ecbedc7f6bf946b84b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 17:33:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 28/30] fix(workspace): env-first town-root resolution prevents
 phantom-town split-brain
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FindFromCwdOrError walked up from CWD looking for mayor/ or mayor/town.json,
and only consulted GT_TOWN_ROOT / GT_ROOT as a last-resort fallback. That made
the env var unreachable whenever any parent dir happened to contain a mayor/
subdir.

Incident (2026-04-23 → 2026-04-24 on anvil): a failed pre-push deploy ssh'd
into anvil with CWD=$HOME and spawned a daemon that scaffolded mayor/,
.beads/, daemon/, rigs.json under /home/hunter. From that point, any shell
rooted at $HOME that invoked 'gt daemon run' (notably deacon's tmux spawn
with PWD=/home/hunter) walked up from CWD, found /home/hunter/mayor, and
started a parallel daemon there — ignoring GT_TOWN_ROOT=/home/hunter/gt.
The phantom ran its own Dolt server and processed molecules/wisps for ~18h
as split-brain with the real town, undetected.

Fix: trust the session manager / agent spawner when it explicitly sets
GT_TOWN_ROOT or GT_ROOT. Validate the path via IsWorkspace before using it.
Only fall back to the CWD walk when no env var is set or the env target
isn't a workspace. Normal agent and shell flows are unchanged; the only
behavior delta is that a stray/phantom mayor/ on the CWD walk path no
longer shadows an explicit env override.

Adds two regression tests: env wins over a phantom CWD town; invalid env
degrades gracefully to the CWD walk.

Also reconciles patches/ with current upstream/main: the prior commit
regenerated patches/ against a stale upstream ref and inadvertently exported
~80 upstream commits as local patches. 'make patches' against the current
upstream/main restores the minimal local-only patch set (28 patches).
